  "description": "Real building requests for search_blocks. Each query passes when all of its top-3 block IDs match `accept` (fnmatch patterns without the minecraft: prefix) and no `reject` pattern appears in the top 8. `top1` pins the first result where the answer is unambiguous. Acceptable sets are deliberately broad: the gate checks relevance, not one fixed order. `max_per_series` caps how many members of one 16-dye-colour series (white_wool ... black_wool) may appear in the top 8; without a colour in the query they are merged into one candidate. `require` lists patterns of which at least one block must appear in the top 8. An entry with `similar_to` instead of (or with) `keywords` checks the palette-similarity ranking.",
